# Macbeth - The Murder of Duncan (Act 2, Scene 2-3)
# A thrilling adaptation of Shakespeare's tragedy

@backdrop data:castle_hall [fadeIn=500]
@char MACBETH sprite=data:macbeth
@char LADY_MACBETH sprite=data:lady_macbeth
@char MACDUFF sprite=data:macduff
@char LENNOX sprite=data:lennox

# Scene: After the murder - Macbeth returns with bloody hands

LADY_MACBETH: [expression=worried,position=right] My husband!

MACBETH: [expression=shocked,position=left]
"""
I have done the deed.
Didst thou not hear a noise?
"""

LADY_MACBETH: [expression=annoyed,position=right]
"""
I heard the owl scream and the crickets cry.
Did not you speak?
"""

MACBETH: [expression=worried,position=left] When?

LADY_MACBETH: [expression=neutral,position=right] Now.

MACBETH: [expression=shocked,position=left] As I descended?

LADY_MACBETH: [expression=neutral,position=right] Ay.

MACBETH: [expression=worried,position=left]
"""
Hark! Who lies in the second chamber?
"""

LADY_MACBETH: [expression=neutral,position=right] Donalbain.

*MACBETH: [cutin=size=large,expression=shocked]
"""
This is a sorry sight!
Methought I heard a voice cry 'Sleep no more!
Macbeth does murder sleep!'
"""

wait 1000

LADY_MACBETH: [expression=annoyed,position=right]
"""
What do you mean?
Consider it not so deeply!
"""

MACBETH: [expression=worried,position=left]
"""
Still it cried 'Sleep no more!' to all the house:
'Glamis hath murdered sleep, and therefore
Cawdor shall sleep no more; Macbeth shall sleep no more.'
"""

LADY_MACBETH: [expression=annoyed,position=right]
"""
Who was it that thus cried? Why, worthy thane,
You do unbend your noble strength to think
So brainsickly of things!
"""

*LADY_MACBETH: [cutin=size=large,expression=angry]
"""
Go get some water and wash this filthy witness from your hand!
Why did you bring these daggers from the place?
They must lie there!
"""

MACBETH: [expression=shocked,position=left]
"""
I'll go no more.
I am afraid to think what I have done;
Look on't again I dare not!
"""

LADY_MACBETH: [expression=angry,position=right]
"""
Infirm of purpose!
Give me the daggers!
"""

@transition fadeOutBackdrop [duration=600]

wait 2000

# Scene: Morning - The discovery

@backdrop data:castle_courtyard [fadeIn=500]

@action MACDUFF moveTo [x=30,duration=400]

MACDUFF: [expression=neutral,position=left]
"""
Is the king stirring, worthy thane?
"""

MACBETH: [expression=worried,position=right] Not yet.

MACDUFF: [expression=neutral,position=left]
"""
He did command me to call timely on him.
I have almost slipped the hour.
"""

MACBETH: [expression=worried,position=right] I'll bring you to him.

wait 1500

*MACDUFF: [cutin=size=large,expression=shocked]
"""
O horror, horror, horror!
Tongue nor heart cannot conceive nor name thee!
"""

MACBETH: [expression=shocked,position=right] What's the matter?

*MACDUFF: [cutin=size=large,expression=shocked]
"""
Confusion now hath made his masterpiece!
Most sacrilegious murder hath broke ope
The Lord's anointed temple and stole thence
The life o' the building!
"""

MACBETH: [expression=shocked,position=right] What is't you say? The life?

LENNOX: [expression=shocked,position=center] Mean you his majesty?

*MACDUFF: [cutin=size=large,expression=sad]
"""
Approach the chamber and destroy your sight
With a new Gorgon. Do not bid me speak!
See, and then speak yourselves!
"""

@action MACBETH moveTo [x=40,duration=500]
@action LENNOX moveTo [x=60,duration=500]

wait 1000

LADY_MACBETH: [expression=worried,position=left]
"""
What's the business,
That such a hideous trumpet calls to parley
The sleepers of the house? Speak, speak!
"""

MACDUFF: [expression=sad,position=right]
"""
O gentle lady,
'Tis not for you to hear what I can speak:
The repetition in a woman's ear
Would murder as it fell!
"""

*MACBETH: [cutin=size=large,expression=worried]
"""
Had I but died an hour before this chance,
I had lived a blessed time; for from this instant
There's nothing serious in mortality!
"""

MACDUFF: [expression=sad,position=left]
"""
Look to the lady!
"""

@transition wipe [duration=800]

# End Scene

@end
